1018
01:02:04,510 --> 01:02:07,810
how is your input
length, for instance

1019
01:02:07,810 --> 01:02:09,410
if you have a
shorter input length.

1020
01:02:09,410 --> 01:02:11,670
So here what we want
to do is to avoid

1021
01:02:11,670 --> 01:02:15,190
having to do all these things
for the whole o of n squared

1022
01:02:15,190 --> 01:02:15,690
thing.

1023
01:02:15,690 --> 01:02:17,790
So I guess all of
these come into play.

1024
01:02:17,790 --> 01:02:19,750
So I would say it's
not straightforward as

1025
01:02:19,750 --> 01:02:21,290
to what the answer should be.

1026
01:02:21,290 --> 01:02:24,330
But I would say a
lot of recent models,

1027
01:02:24,330 --> 01:02:29,050
they tend to share
projection matrices.

1028
01:02:29,050 --> 01:02:31,570
So typically, I would say
GQA is what you would see.

1029
01:02:31,570 --> 01:02:34,400
But it's not necessarily
the case for all models.

1030
01:02:34,400 --> 01:02:36,970

1031
01:02:36,970 --> 01:02:37,470
Cool.

1032
01:02:37,470 --> 01:02:38,610
